    <briefdescription>
<para>Struct representing a named boolean constant, created by the <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-literals_1gad4203783cfbe141f41ee8515f7b2ea94" kindref="member">_b</ref></computeroutput> literal. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1named__bool" kindref="compound">named_bool</ref></computeroutput> struct holds the constant <computeroutput>true</computeroutput>, together with a name, which the expression formatter prints instead of the value, so that a failed comparison like <computeroutput>"flag"<ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-literals_1gad4203783cfbe141f41ee8515f7b2ea94" kindref="member">_b</ref> == flag</computeroutput>, with the operators in the <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1operators" kindref="compound">operators</ref></computeroutput> namespace, is reported as <computeroutput>flag == false</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>The value is available only via the implicit conversion to <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>, and the struct has neither a <computeroutput>get()</computeroutput> accessor nor comparison operators. Thus <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a59eb53c96f68d26635c13df53b358ac8" kindref="member">detail::unwrap()</ref></computeroutput> returns the object itself, so that the formatter receives the name, the comparators compare it as the <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput> value <computeroutput>true</computeroutput>, and the generic operators in the <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1operators" kindref="compound">operators</ref></computeroutput> namespace, not a better matching operator of this struct, are selected for it.</para>
<para>The name is not owned; it refers to the string literal, which has static storage duration. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
